WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.090
- I hear you travel around in an RV,

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:02.923
which I love.
- Yeah. (laughs)

00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:03.756
- We have an RV.

00:00:03.756 --> 00:00:04.589
We have a Cyclone,

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:05.422
my husband and I.
- Really?

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:06.860
Really?
- Yes! It's fun, yeah.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.897
- Years ago, I bought
one and my niece said,

00:00:09.897 --> 00:00:12.150
"Well, I guess it's the
boomer thing to do".

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.940
You know? Which was like--
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.390
But, what I loved about it,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.590
is we traveled all over the
United States, you know?

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.530
Cracker Barrel!

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.363
- I love Cracker Barrel.

00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:21.751
- We would go to cracker barrels

00:00:21.751 --> 00:00:23.240
and what I loved about it,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.260
is I could just be real, you know?

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.093
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:27.740
- People were at times complimentary,

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.570
but there's no filter and we can just,

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.115
you know, they weren't impressed.

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.020
- [Kelly] I love that!

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.150
- I know.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.270
I remember being in Idaho,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.930
and there was a Native American guy

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.940
and he came over to the table

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.900
and he had this beautiful,
very simple turquoise necklace

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.760
and I commented on it and he took it off

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.270
and put it on my neck.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.174
And--

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:50.327
- Good thing you didn't
compliment his pants.

00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:52.744
(all laugh)

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.000
Just, wow!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.040
I'm just saying.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.147
I see where this is
going and I'm like whoa!

00:01:00.147 --> 00:01:01.560
Just putting it on you!

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.100
- I'm taking this, and then I'm going.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.080
Okay, no, but cool thing about it was,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.410
he explained that that's
what Indian giving means.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.410
- Oh, the real meaning?

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.947
- The real meaning of
it because we often say,

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:14.060
"You're an Indian giver"
and that's not it.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.750
- [Kelly] Yeah, I always
find that very offensive.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.583
- I know.

00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:18.910
If you compliment, you
have to give it to them,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.570
and that's Indian giving.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.500
- Oh, my gosh!

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.820
I compliment people all the time.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.132
I would have so many things.

00:01:24.132 --> 00:01:24.965
(audience laughing)

00:01:24.965 --> 00:01:27.270
I love complimenting people
because you meet people,

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.120
especially like fans and stuff and--

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.420
- Well, I loved your earrings.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.095
- Exactly, here you go.
(all laughing)

00:01:33.095 --> 00:01:35.210
But, do you still use the RV?

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.960
- No, it's in storage.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.463
I used it on the Warner Brother's lot,

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.593
but the driver and I broke up.

00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:45.467
- Oh, no! Oh, no!
(both laughing)

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.560
- You are making me cry with laughter.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.393
I swear to god.
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:49.393 --> 00:01:51.040
Oh, my gosh! That's my eye that waters.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:51.920
We have so much in common.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:52.812
- [Kathy] I know!

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.829
(all laughing)

00:01:53.829 --> 00:01:55.079
♪ Sisters ♪

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:56.526
♪ Sisters ♪

00:01:56.526 --> 00:01:57.643
- I know that song!

00:01:57.643 --> 00:01:58.787
That's my favorite!

00:01:58.787 --> 00:02:00.543
Oh, I love you, okay.

